    "chalk_eraser_comment": "Easter egg (MILESTONES D14): a chalkboard eraser dropped in the fountain park south of the bell tower (workspace.Arena.ChalkEraser). Shoot it = a chalk cloud `radius` studs round a point a little above it for `seconds`; planes inside it are hard to see and can't be locked, aimed at with assist, chased by bots or name-tagged. Radius 2.25x then +30% and cooldown 3 min -> 2 min after Alan's playtests (2026-10-15). The felt is black after a puff and slowly turns chalky white; white = ready. Lasts 45 s (was 20, then 30), radius 20% smaller (364 -> 291), sight blocked through it like a building; full size for the first half, then shrinks to 15% and is gone (Rules.chalkRadius); inside, fog limits sight to about 380 studs. Ready again `cooldown_seconds` after a puff.",
    "chalk_eraser": {"radius": 291, "seconds": 45, "cooldown_seconds": 120},
    "ducts_comment": "Escape ducts above the drop ceiling (MILESTONES D14; layout redone as a maze after Alan's look, 2026-10-15). `rooms` (240 across) are the bends and junctions; `links` join two rooms on a straight line, ducts `width` wide and `height` tall from the ceiling top at `floor_y`. Four `vents` (ceiling holes `vent` across) at irregular spots; every vent reaches every other, with loops. The ducts pass over five of the classroom's ceiling lights: their glow comes up through grilles, the only light inside. `pipe`: one link is a round pipe `diameter` across the whole way (the heavy gunship, 26 wide, can't fit; others, 18.5 wide at most, can if they fly it straight). `fans`: spinning fans across ducts at `spots` [x, z, duct direction, way the air blows (+1/-1 along it)] in a round housing `opening` across (blades `reach` from the middle, inside the duct); a plane whose middle crosses a blade (`blade_width` + `plane_margin`) or the hub loses `damage_share` of its health and is shoved sideways. Moving air: flying with a fan's air speeds you up by up to `wind`; against it slows you by `headwind_share` of that (easier to time the blades; Alan: against was a little too slow); the `blower` in its room blows the same way along its `link`, stronger. Built by tools/ducts.py into assets/models/ducts.model.json; the server lets planes fly up to the duct roof.",
